            <ArticleTitle>Burning mouth syndrome and vulvodynia coexisting in the same patient: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>75-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The 'dynias' are a group of chronic focal pain syndromes with a predilection for the orocervical and urogenital regions. This is a case report of stomatodynia (burning mouth syndrome) and vulvodynia coexisting in a middle-aged woman. The dynias are an enigma in terms of aetiology, which is multifactorial, making clinical investigations difficult and often requiring liaison with other specialties.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
